A||||6||4Banger Bandit||Greetings... Got some Iron Duke questions...
Z||000000||4Banger Bandit||07-28-99||08:38 PM||||Hello everyone.  I fairly recently purchased an '84 Fiero in reletively good shape.  I just kinda bought the car to keep the miles off my 94-Z28, but I've grown to like the Fiero pretty well.  I like the idea of "hoppin'-up" this Iron Duck, and I'm wondering if anyone has tried the Holley products like the intake manifolds and carbs for these 2.5L "beasts."(chuckle..) So far I've just given the car a pretty major tune-up, and it seems to run pretty strong, aside from a slightly erratic idle.  Has anybody done the non-computer carb setup??  I'm toying with the idea of ditching the computer and going fully carbed.  What does everyone think?<p>-jeff
Z||000001||batboy||07-28-99||09:03 PM||||One of my Fieros is a four cylinder 2.5 Iron Duke, which I really liked until it recently died (rod went out). There are some past discussions about possible upgrades to this engine, but I think the majority of us think that high performance and the 2.5 engine do not mix. The hot rodders among us go with the V6 or in rare cases, the V8 like my other Fiero (da batmobile). If you want to prove me wrong, try looking at this web site.<p>http://www.amotion.com/p4.html
Z||000002||4Banger Bandit||07-28-99||11:16 PM||||I just get-off on the idea of making the Iron Duke into something more.  It's just a cute little engine... I've got the part numbers for the Holley TBI unit... Happen to know a good place to order Holley products on the web?
Z||000003||Cooter||07-29-99||07:15 AM||||Fourbanger- Summit can get the Holley throttle body and it is a lot less expensive than buying it from Fiero Store
Z||000004||ChadMan||07-29-99||02:05 PM||||V6 Fieros are great, and I love mine, but I love the 4-bangers too, and I don't think they get the respect they deserve.  They're cheap to own and operate, they're easy to work on, and they make as much or more power than "real" sports cars like MG's, Triumphs, the original Porsche Speedster, and the original RX-7.<p>Having said that, you'll have a hard time getting more than 115 hp out of a Duke unless you go Super Duty, which is really expensive.  If you want a hot 4-banger, why not consider a Quad-4 swap?
Z||000005||lowCG||07-30-99||12:05 AM||||When I had my 4cyl car,I almost put a set of Weber carbs on,would've needed a 290DEG cam,and Old sunbird HEI as well.<br>Was curious to find out if anyone has done anything like this?
Z||000006||Racer 1||08-04-99||01:49 AM||||Get hooker headers for the 2.5.I have the super competion headers "tri" y you can also get the "4 into 1" header also which I wish I had gotten.you can also get NOS, and ball bearing rocker arms for the "IRON DUCK"..I also polished my TBI on the inside.If you get the holley throttle body please post if there was a big difference from the stock Throttle body.Call summit racing and PAW performance automotive warehouse.I like my 4 banger its alot more easy to work on then the v-6's.........
